        "submissionFlow": "Employee Login → Create Report → Add Lines (category/date/amount/receipt) → Add Attendees → Submit → Supervisor Approval → Finance Review → Expense Report Export → AP Invoice → Payment",
        "sourceFilter": "NonValidatedWebExpense (distinguishes iExpense from direct AP entries in ap_invoices_all)"
      },
      "learningObjectives": [
        "Configure iExpense System Options and expense categories",
        "Set up expense policies (amount limits, receipt requirements)",
        "Process expense report submission and approval workflow",
        "Integrate corporate card transactions",
        "Process cash advances and apply to expense reports",
        "Query expense reports with policy violations",
        "Troubleshoot expense reimbursement issues"
      ],
      "relatesTo": [
        "ebs:iEXP",
        "ebs:AP",
        "ebs:HRMS",
        "ebs:P2P_Process"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ebs:ModuleKnowledge_FixedAssets",
      "type": "ModuleKnowledge",
      "name": "Oracle Fixed Assets Complete Guide",
      "description": "Complete FA guide — Asset Book Types (Corporate/Tax/Budget), Depreciation Methods (STL/DDB/SYD/ACRS/MACRS/UNIT_PROD), Asset Lifecycle (Add→Depreciate→Transfer→Retire), CIP assets, Mass Additions from AP, Retirement accounting entries.",
      "identityKey": "knowledgeId: FA-FUNC-001",
      "humanRef": "topicName",
      "attributes": {
        "knowledgeId": "FA-FUNC-001",
        "moduleCode": "FA",
        "topicName": "Oracle Fixed Assets Complete Setup and Processing",
        "topicCategory": "FUNCTIONAL",
        "difficulty": "ADVANCED",
        "businessProcess": "R2R",
        "depreciationMethods": "STL: Straight Line; DDB: Double Declining Balance; SYD: Sum of Years Digits; ACRS: Accelerated Cost Recovery; MACRS: Modified ACRS; UNIT_PROD: Units of Production; NBV_RSL: Net Book Value Remaining Life",
        "assetTypes": "CAPITALIZED: Active depreciating asset; CIP: Construction in Progress (no depreciation); EXPENSED: Below capitalize threshold",
        "massAdditionsFlow": "AP Invoice for capital item → Create Accounting in AP → Run Mass Additions Create → Review in FA_MASS_ADDITIONS → Post Mass Additions → Assets created in FA",
        "retirementAccounting": "DR: Accumulated Depreciation / DR: Proceeds of Sale / CR: Asset Cost Account / CR/DR: Gain or Loss on Disposal"
      },
      "learningObjectives": [
        "Configure asset books, categories, and depreciation methods",
        "Add assets manually and via Mass Additions from AP",
        "Execute monthly depreciation (FADPRUN) and create journals",
        "Process asset transfers between departments/locations",
        "Retire assets (full, partial, mass) with gain/loss calculation",
        "Track CIP assets and capitalize on completion",
        "Query asset register with NBV and remaining life"
      ],
      "relatesTo": [
        "ebs:FA",
        "ebs:AP",
        "ebs:GL",
        "ebs:R2R_Process"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ebs:ModuleKnowledge_AdvancedPLSQL",
      "type": "ModuleKnowledge",
      "name": "Advanced PL/SQL Patterns for Oracle EBS",
      "description": "Advanced PL/SQL guide — BULK COLLECT and FORALL for high-performance batch processing, UTL_FILE for CSV/log file processing, DBMS_SCHEDULER for job automation, autonomous transactions for audit trails, dynamic SQL with bind variables, pipelined functions for large result sets.",
      "identityKey": "knowledgeId: PLSQL-ADV-001",
      "humanRef": "topicName",
      "attributes": {
        "knowledgeId": "PLSQL-ADV-001",
        "moduleCode": "TECH",
        "topicName": "Advanced PL/SQL Patterns for Oracle EBS",
        "topicCategory": "TECHNICAL",
        "difficulty": "EXPERT",
        "keyPatterns": "BULK COLLECT / FORALL: Process 1000+ rows per batch for maximum performance; UTL_FILE: Read/write flat files from EBS server directories; DBMS_SCHEDULER: Schedule concurrent-like jobs with logging; AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION: Audit trail without rollback risk; EXECUTE IMMEDIATE with USING: Dynamic SQL with bind variables; PIPELINED FUNCTION: Stream large result sets without memory overflow"
      },
      "learningObjectives": [
        "Implement BULK COLLECT / FORALL for high-performance batch processing",
        "Use UTL_FILE for flat file processing with proper error handling",
        "Implement error handling with PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION for audit trails",
        "Write safe dynamic SQL using EXECUTE IMMEDIATE with bind variables",
        "Create pipelined functions for streaming large data sets",
        "Implement DBMS_SCHEDULER jobs with logging and retry logic"
      ],
      "relatesTo": [
        "ebs:AP",
        "ebs:GL",
        "ebs:HRMS",
        "ebs:EBSExtension_APUtilsPackage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ebs:ModuleKnowledge_Troubleshooting",
      "type": "ModuleKnowledge",
      "name": "Oracle EBS Complete Troubleshooting Guide",
      "description": "Complete troubleshooting guide for Oracle EBS — 8 issue types: (1) AP Invoice Stuck on Hold with diagnosis queries and resolution matrix, (2) GL Journal Not Posting, (3) Workflow Stuck Notification, (4) Concurrent Program Failure, (5) Interface Import Failures, (6) Performance Issues, (7) HRMS DateTrack Errors, (8) Inventory Negative Balance.",
      "identityKey": "knowledgeId: TROUBLE-001",
      "humanRef": "topicName",
      "attributes": {
        "knowledgeId": "TROUBLE-001",
        "moduleCode": "TECH",
        "topicName": "Oracle EBS Complete Troubleshooting Guide",
        "topicCategory": "TROUBLESHOOTING",
        "difficulty": "EXPERT",
        "issueTypes": "AP Invoice Stuck on Hold (QTY ORD, PRICE, DIST VARIANCE, NO RATE, INVALID ACCOUNT, FUTURE PERIOD); GL Journal Not Posting (Period Closed, Debit/Credit Imbalance, Invalid Account, Budget Control, CVR Failure); Workflow Stuck Notification (Email missing, ERROR status retry, Reassign, Cancel and restart); Concurrent Program Failure (ORA-01555 Snapshot Too Old, ORA-04031 Shared Pool, ORA-01652 Temp Space); Interface Import Failures (AP Invoice Interface, GL Interface, AR AutoInvoice Interface errors); Performance Issues (Slow SQL, Missing org_id, Functions on indexes, Stale statistics, DBMS_STATS); HRMS DateTrack Errors (Multiple rows, incorrect aggregations, wrong headcount); Inventory Negative Balance (Pending transactions, cycle count, parameter check)",
        "keyDiagnosticTables": "ap_holds_all; gl_posting_interim; wf_errors; fnd_concurrent_requests; ap_interface_rejections; v$sql; mtl_material_transactions_temp"
      },
      "troubleshootingGuide": "For AP Invoice Hold: Query ap_holds_all WHERE release_lookup_code IS NULL. For GL Not Posting: Check gl_period_statuses closing_status and verify running_total_dr = running_total_cr. For Workflow Stuck: Query wf_item_activity_statuses_v WHERE activity_status IN ('NOTIFIED','ERROR','ACTIVE') — use wf_engine.handleerror for retry. For Concurrent Failure: Check fnd_concurrent_requests logfile_name and review ORA error in log. For Performance: Always include org_id, use bind variables, avoid TO_CHAR/TRUNC on indexed columns.",
      "relatesTo": [
        "ebs:AP",
        "ebs:GL",
        "ebs:HRMS",
        "ebs:INV",
        "ebs:Workflow_APInvoiceApproval"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ebs:ModuleKnowledge_InterviewQuestions",
      "type": "ModuleKnowledge",
      "name": "Oracle EBS Complete Interview Questions Guide",
      "description": "Comprehensive Oracle EBS interview question bank — AP (10 questions: invoice types, matching, period close, payment batch, holds), GL (8 questions: Primary vs Secondary Ledger, XLA, FSG, cross validation, suspense), AR (6 questions: AutoInvoice, AutoCash, Lockbox, revenue recognition), P2P (3 questions: complete cycle, Blanket PO, Finally Closed), O2C (3 questions), HRMS (5+ questions: DateTrack, enterprise structure, APIs), Technical (10+ questions: FND_GLOBAL, WHO columns, FNDLOAD, Flexfields, Patching).",
      "identityKey": "knowledgeId: INTERVIEW-001",
      "humanRef": "topicName",
      "attributes": {
        "knowledgeId": "INTERVIEW-001",
        "moduleCode": "ALL",
        "topicName": "Complete Oracle EBS Interview Questions",
        "topicCategory": "LEARNING",
        "difficulty": "ALL_LEVELS"
      },
      "interviewQuestions": [
        "Q: What are the different invoice types in Oracle AP? A: Standard, Credit Memo, Debit Memo, Prepayment, Expense Report, Interest, Mixed, QuickDefault",
        "Q: Explain 2-way, 3-way, 4-way PO matching. A: 2-way=Invoice+PO only; 3-way=Invoice+PO+Receipt; 4-way=Invoice+PO+Receipt+Inspection",
        "Q: What is the difference between Primary and Secondary Ledger? A: Primary is the main GAAP ledger; Secondary is for reporting in different currency/COA/SLA method (e.g. IFRS vs Local GAAP)",
        "Q: Explain Subledger Accounting (SLA/XLA) flow. A: Subledger Transaction → xla_events → xla_ae_headers → xla_ae_lines → GL Transfer → gl_je_headers/lines → gl_balances",
        "Q: What is DateTrack and what filter is mandatory? A: HRMS mechanism to preserve all history. Mandatory filter: SYSDATE BETWEEN effective_start_date AND effective_end_date",
        "Q: What is AutoInvoice and how does it work? A: Imports invoices from OM/PA/custom into AR via ra_interface_lines_all → AutoInvoice Import → ra_customer_trx_all",
        "Q: What is ATP in Order Management? A: Available to Promise — checks On-hand + Supply - Demand = Available Qty for customer delivery date promise",
        "Q: Explain complete P2P accounting entries. A: PR Approval: DR Requisition Encumb/CR Budgetary; PO: DR Obligation/CR Encumb; Receipt: DR Recv Inspection/CR AP Accrual; Invoice Match: DR AP Accrual/CR AP Liability; Payment: DR AP Liability/CR Cash Clearing; Bank Clear: DR Cash Clearing/CR Bank",
        "Q: What is FND_GLOBAL and its key functions? A: Session context package — USER_ID, LOGIN_ID, RESP_ID, ORG_ID, EMPLOYEE_ID, CONC_REQUEST_ID",
        "Q: What are WHO columns and why are they required? A: CREATED_BY, CREATION_DATE, LAST_UPDATED_BY, LAST_UPDATE_DATE, LAST_UPDATE_LOGIN — required for Oracle support and audit compliance"
      ],
      "relatesTo": [
        "ebs:AP",
        "ebs:GL",
        "ebs:AR",
        "ebs:HRMS",
        "ebs:PO",
        "ebs:OM"
      ]
    },
